WEBVTT

00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:01.056
Here's the problem.

00:00:01.392 --> 00:00:03.343
A bare template has no new strand.

00:00:03.796 --> 00:00:05.734
DNA polymerase can't begin here.

00:00:06.129 --> 00:00:07.859
It needs a 3-prime end to add

00:00:07.905 --> 00:00:08.277
to.

00:00:08.614 --> 00:00:09.995
So primase steps in.

00:00:10.286 --> 00:00:12.178
It lays down a short RNA primer.

00:00:12.631 --> 00:00:14.012
Think of it as a starter block.

00:00:14.349 --> 00:00:16.276
Now polymerase has a 3-prime end.

00:00:16.613 --> 00:00:18.273
It extends the primer with DNA.

00:00:18.900 --> 00:00:20.352
Now try the question again.
